I'm using this in two case, one is MAVSDK/C++ and the other is MAVSDK-Server & C#.
Both of two cases, battery info. shows incorrect value. If I connect the 16V battery, it shows like this

In MAVSDK-Server & C# 

```
{ "voltageV": 15.1, "remainingPercent": 0.51 }
{ "voltageV": 15.1, "remainingPercent": 0.51 }
{ "voltageV": 3.775, "remainingPercent": 0.51 }
{ "voltageV": 3.775, "remainingPercent": 0.51 }
{ "voltageV": 3.775, "remainingPercent": 0.51 }
{ "voltageV": 3.775, "remainingPercent": 0.51 }
{ "voltageV": 3.775, "remainingPercent": 0.51 }
```

Beginning of some callbacks, it shows right value, but a few seconds later battery voltage is something wrong. Looks like one cell's voltage. In use of MAVSDK/C++, shows same result. So, my case - MAVSDK/C++ - I used the "mavlink_passthrough" plugin like this.

```
bool DroneModel_Impl::onPassthruIncomingMessageAsync(mavlink_message_t message)
{
  if (telemetry_armed_)
  {
    // logging here
  }

  if (message.msgid == MAVLINK_MSG_ID_RC_CHANNELS)
  {
    manual_control_ = (mavlink_msg_rc_channels_get_chan8_raw(&message) >= kForcedManualControlRcRaw);
  }
  else if (message.msgid == MAVLINK_MSG_ID_BATTERY_STATUS)
  {
    mavlink_battery_status_t  battery_status;
    float   voltage = 0.0f;

    mavlink_msg_battery_status_decode(&message, &battery_status);

    for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++)
    {
      if (battery_status.voltages[i] = UINT16_MAX)
        break;
      voltage += static_cast<float>(battery_status.voltages[i]) * 0.001f;
    }

    if (battery_status.id == 0)       tether_voltage_ = voltage;
    else if (battery_status.id == 1)  battery_voltage_ = voltage;
  }

  return true;
}
```

But MAVSDK-Server & C#, I think it can not access the raw mavlink message, isn't it?

Actually, I used the two power pack system. But same result that use only one power pack system. Telemetry plugin's Battery information is incorrect, my guess. Am I wrong? How can I get the battery voltage correctly?

